Z||000000||8Ball||08-06-2001||04:38 PM||||Well while out trying to sell networking services for the shop where I am working, I stopped at Malibu Collision. They do custom Paint jobs ect ect ect. And I must say from what I saw in the shop they do some of the most AMAZEING work I have seen in a long time.<P>Well they are haveing me install a network soon, but anyway back to the story. I asked just for future referance, how much a paint job would cost me. Base color on a Fiero of Purple pearl With a flame job done in BASF Extreme Color (that chameleon color) The flames would stop at the windshield and go halfway back on the doors. It would look SWEET. But he quoted me the price at 3500 complete. Not a bad price for the quality work they do.<P>If anyone in the tennesse area would like to see some of their work go to <A HREF="http://www.malibucollision.com" TARGET=_blank>www.malibucollision.com</A> <P>They do some AWSOME work!!!<BR>So one of these days when I get a Fiero and save up the money for the paint they will be putting on my dream paint job  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Randy||||reg||1
Z||000001||saleenfiero||08-06-2001||06:53 PM||||What does that chameleon color cost to paint a car?  I'm not talking any flames or anything, is it alot more than normal paint?  Anyone?  C'mon shoot, shoot me some info||||reg||1
Z||000002||8Ball||08-06-2001||09:33 PM||||the cost of JUST the paint is $298-$500 a pint. so yea it usually costs triple to paint a car with it around here. At least.<BR>Randy||||reg||1
Z||000003||beer_stud_21||08-06-2001||11:56 PM||||$500.00 a pint!!!! Fuggin A!  There are enough real chameleons around here I could do it way cheaper than that.  Enough time and a big bottle of super glue.  Only problem being they only come in chameleon green and chaleleon brown.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||08-07-2001||12:12 AM||||You guys are all getting ripped off royally. the top coat is all that gets it,like a 3 stage pearl. so with an HVLP gun you can do the whole car after you apply the base with a pint. Then just clear over it. Its only an added single step, like an extra coat of color. And it costs far less than that. Even the Maaco next door does them for $300 and up. If you pay $300-$500 a can for it, Ive got a Fiero with a Ferrari kit that ill sell you for $75,000 and its Ferrari Rossa Corsa red.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||10
